# The edition operator as a module (issue #706 §4): the edition CORE
# operator, bound — not redefined. `ed` is RESERVED (the machinery's
# token); a body binds its edition spelling through this module's faces.
#
# An edition is an identity fact of one document (the second edition of
# THIS document), not a wrapper: the module declares no identity
# composition — the operator binds to the edition attribute of the
# composing definition's type.

module: edition.core
version: 1
title: "The edition operator"
description: >-
  The core edition operator as a binding: the edition ordinal of the
  document itself. The module declares the generic edition faces; the
  body's spelling (ed 2, Ed. 3, 2017-ed-2) binds through the composing
  definition.

grammar:
  # edition_space (the separator between the operator word and the
  # ordinal) is supplied by the composing definition's grammar: it is a
  # body face, not a core one.
  edition_ordinal: '1*digit'
  edition_face: '"ed" edition_space edition_ordinal'

hooks:
  edition_semantics: >-
    The edition-of relation (dated_version_of?, the edition attribute) is
    core machinery. Bodies with edition-bearing legacy faces bind the
    spelling, never the semantics.
